    %% SQL Query Processing Flow
    Note over Client,Cloud: GPU/SIMD-Accelerated SQL Processing
    
    Client->>+REST: POST /query<br/> SQL with VECTOR_SIMILARITY
    REST->>+SQL: execute_sql()<br/> Complex vector query
    
    SQL->>+HW: get_hardware_capabilities()<br/> Check available acceleration
    HW-->>-SQL: GPU: CUDA, CPU: AVX2<br/> Hardware profile
    
    alt GPU Available
        SQL->>+GPU: parse_sql_gpu()<br/> "SELECT * FROM collection<br/>ORDER BY VECTOR_SIMILARITY(vector, [0.1, 0.2], 'cosine')"
        GPU->>+HW: has_gpu_parsing()<br/> Check GPU parsing enabled
        HW-->>-GPU: true
        GPU->>GPU: tokenize_gpu()<br/> CUDA/ROCm/MPS/OpenCL
        GPU->>GPU: parse_tokens_cpu()<br/> Grammar processing
        GPU-->>-SQL: ParsedQuery<br/> 0.8ms parse time
    else GPU Unavailable
        SQL->>+SIMD: parse_vector_array()<br/> "[0.1, 0.2, 0.3, ...]"
        SIMD->>+HW: has_simd()<br/> Check SIMD capabilities
        HW-->>-SIMD: AVX2 available
        SIMD->>SIMD: parse_avx2()<br/> 8 elements per instruction
        SIMD-->>-SQL: Vec<f32><br/> 163.3 MB/s throughput
    end
    
    SQL->>+DVS: search_vectors()<br/> Optimized query execution
    DVS->>+Engine: search_with_metadata()<br/> Hardware-aware search
    Engine-->>-DVS: Vector results
    DVS-->>-SQL: Ranked results
    SQL-->>-REST: Query results
    REST-->>-Client: JSON response<br/> Sub-2ms query time
    
